window.FD = {"study":{"readings":[{"n":"01","title":"Marriage and family","parts":[{"title":"Love and responsibility","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["Notice who is addressed. Paul does not tell husbands to make their wives submit, or wives to make their husbands love. Each person is handed their own instruction, and it is given in front of the others. Paul opens with submission to one another out of reverence for Christ (",{"r":"EPH.5.21","t":"Ephesians 5:21"},"), then speaks to wives and husbands in turn: wives are to submit as to the Lord, because the husband is the head of the wife as Christ is the head of the church; husbands are to love as Christ loved the church and gave himself up for her (",{"r":"EPH.5.22-33","t":"Ephesians 5:22–33"},")."]},{"k":"quote","t":"Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ loved the church and gave Himself up for her","r":"EPH.5.25","label":"Ephesians 5:25"},{"k":"p","runs":["Paul's reason for this reaches back to the beginning. He quotes ",{"r":"GEN.2.24","t":"Genesis 2:24"}," on the two becoming one flesh, and says the mystery concerns Christ and the church (",{"r":"EPH.5.31-32","t":"Ephesians 5:31–32"},"). Marriage, on this reading, is not an arrangement people invented. The Baptist Faith and Message, the confession this site writes under, calls it \"the uniting of one man and one woman in covenant commitment for a lifetime\", and holds husband and wife of equal worth before God, the husband to love and lead his family and the wife graciously to submit to his servant leadership (Article 18)."]},{"k":"care","runs":["How does verse 21 fit with what follows? This is the hard question in the passage, and this is the reading this site follows, with its reason from the text. Verse 21 calls all believers to submit to one another; verses 22 to 33 then speak to wives and husbands differently, and the two instructions are not exchanged. ",{"r":"COL.3.18-19","t":"Colossians 3:18–19"}," gives the same two instructions without the sentence about one another, which suggests they are not simply a restatement of it."]},{"k":"source","src":"calvin-eph","runs":["Calvin reads verse 21 as a real and universal duty, \"mutual subjection\", then says Paul \"comes now to the various conditions of life\", beginning with the \"yoke of marriage\". So the general call and the particular callings stand together."]},{"k":"source","src":"gill","runs":["John Gill, an eighteenth-century Baptist pastor, keeps the limit and the tone in view. A wife's submission is \"not in anything that is contrary to the laws of God and Christ; for God is to be obeyed rather than men\", and it \"is not a servile one\"."]},{"k":"other","runs":["Some Christians read this differently. They take verse 21 to govern everything after it, so that husband and wife lead and submit alike and headship carries no distinct responsibility of leading. That view is theirs, and it is not the view of the confession this site writes under. This draft has not yet read a named source arguing it, so it quotes none."]},{"k":"p","runs":["Colossians adds one plain command: husbands are not to be harsh with their wives (",{"r":"COL.3.19","t":"Colossians 3:19"},"). This passage can never be a licence for cruelty. Gill says that \"bitter language, threatening words, sour looks, and especially bitter blows\" are \"cruel, churlish, barbarous, and brutish, unbecoming the man and the Christian\". If someone at home is hurting you or you are afraid, getting to safety and asking for help does not disobey these verses; if you are in danger now, contact your local emergency services. Those last words are this site's application, not a quotation from Paul, and this study is not professional guidance."]}]},{"title":"Children and those bringing them up","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["Children are told to obey their parents in the Lord, and Paul quotes the commandment to honour father and mother with its promise (",{"r":"EPH.6.1-3","t":"Ephesians 6:1–3"},", quoting ",{"r":"EXO.20.12","t":"Exodus 20:12"},"). Then he turns straight to the adult: fathers are not to provoke their children to wrath, but to bring them up in the discipline and instruction of the Lord (",{"r":"EPH.6.4","t":"Ephesians 6:4"},"). Colossians gives a reason a parent can feel: so that they will not become discouraged (",{"r":"COL.3.20-21","t":"Colossians 3:20–21"},")."]},{"k":"p","runs":["The child's duty does not cancel the adult's. If children are in your care, you might ask whether your correction teaches patiently or only lets out your anger. That question is an application, not a command from Paul."]},{"k":"p","runs":["These instructions speak to people who are married or who have children. They do not say that everyone must marry or have children to live faithfully; Paul himself calls his unmarried life a gift (",{"r":"1CO.7.7-8","t":"1 Corinthians 7:7–8"},")."]}]}],"slug":"home","hook":["Everyone in the house is spoken to. Nobody is only spoken about."],"line":["Husband, wife, child and parent each hear their own instruction, and each hears the reason."],"read":["EPH.5.21-6.4","COL.3.18-21"],"says":["Wives are to submit to their husbands; husbands are to love their wives as Christ loved the church; children are to obey; fathers are not to provoke."],"setting":["Letters written to be read out in the churches (",{"r":"COL.4.16","t":"Colossians 4:16"},"), so each person could hear the instruction given to the others. The marriage paragraph is shaped throughout by Christ and the church."],"respond":["Look at one responsibility that is yours at home, and begin with your own conduct rather than a demand on someone else."],"look":["What is each person told, and what reason is each one given? What does the comparison with Christ add to what a husband's love means?"],"response":["Name one act of care, respect or patient instruction that belongs to you at home. Begin with your own conduct."],"verseCount":21},{"n":"02","title":"Work and integrity","parts":[{"title":"Working so that we can share","blocks":[{"k":"quote","t":"He who has been stealing must steal no longer, but must work, doing good with his own hands, that he may have something to share with the one in need.","r":"EPH.4.28","label":"Ephesians 4:28"},{"k":"p","runs":["Follow the movement in that one sentence: from taking what is another person's, to honest work, to giving. The reason for the work is someone else's need."]},{"k":"p","runs":["First Thessalonians sets quiet work beside brotherly love, and gives its reason in how outsiders see believers (",{"r":"1TH.4.9-12","t":"1 Thessalonians 4:9–12"},"). Second Thessalonians speaks to people who will not work and have become busybodies. Paul's wording is \"unwilling\": \"If anyone is unwilling to work, he shall not eat.\" It does not call every person without paid work disobedient, and it says nothing against those who cannot work (",{"r":"2TH.3.6-12","t":"2 Thessalonians 3:6–12"},")."]},{"k":"p","runs":["Then the same passage guards the manner of correction. Do not grow weary in doing good. Do not associate with the one who will not obey, so that he may be ashamed, and yet warn him as a brother, not as an enemy (",{"r":"2TH.3.13-15","t":"2 Thessalonians 3:13–15"},")."]}]},{"title":"Reading the slavery passages honestly","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["Ephesians and Colossians speak to slaves and masters. Do not read \"employee\" and \"employer\" here. Ephesians itself says \"whether he is slave or free\" (",{"r":"EPH.6.8","t":"Ephesians 6:8"},"), and swapping the words would hide what the passage is dealing with."]},{"k":"source","src":"calvin-eph","runs":["Calvin saw this difference in the sixteenth century. Those addressed \"were not hired servants, like those of the present day, but slaves\"."]},{"k":"p","runs":["The instructions ask for sincere service, not service only while being watched. They speak just as directly to masters: give up threats, supply what is right and fair, and remember that the same Master is over you both, with no favouritism (",{"r":"EPH.6.5-9","t":"Ephesians 6:5–9"},"; ",{"r":"COL.3.22-4.1","t":"Colossians 3:22–4:1"},"). These passages govern conduct inside an existing relationship; they must not be used to defend owning people. The same New Testament condemns slave traders (",{"r":"1TI.1.10","t":"1 Timothy 1:10"},"), and Paul sends Onesimus back to Philemon \"no longer as a slave, but better than a slave, as a beloved brother\" (",{"r":"PHM.1.16","t":"Philemon 1:16"},")."]},{"k":"p","runs":["Southern Baptists have reason to read this carefully. In 1995 the Convention named \"the role that slavery played in the formation of the Southern Baptist Convention\", acknowledged that many early Southern Baptists defended slave ownership, rejected slavery as a historic evil, and said \"we genuinely repent of racism of which we have been guilty\"."]},{"k":"p","runs":["Some of this does carry across to your work: honesty when no one is watching, fairness, and answering to God for how you use authority. That is this site's application across very different circumstances, and it is marked as one. So is this: your worth is not measured by your wage or your rank."]}]}],"slug":"work","hook":["A thief puts down what he stole, and picks up something to give."],"line":["Honest work is given a purpose beyond the worker: having something to share."],"read":["EPH.4.28","1TH.4.9-12","2TH.3.6-15","EPH.6.5-9","COL.3.22-4.1"],"says":["Stop stealing and work, so as to have something to share; live quietly and earn your own living; slaves are to serve sincerely, and masters are to give up threats and do what is right and fair."],"setting":["Two different things. Some passages are about ordinary labour and provision. Others address slaves and masters in a world where people were owned, which is not the same as being employed."],"respond":["Take one task you can do with more honesty or care. If you direct other people's work, examine your own fairness first."],"look":["What purpose for work does ",{"r":"EPH.4.28","t":"Ephesians 4:28"}," give? What is demanded of masters, and what is lost if the passage is read only as advice to employees?"],"response":["Choose one task you can carry out with more honesty or care. If you direct others, examine how you use that authority."],"verseCount":25},{"n":"03","title":"Money and generosity","parts":[{"title":"Giving from what we have","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["Paul tells of churches in \"deep poverty\" who pleaded for the privilege of sharing (",{"r":"2CO.8.1-5","t":"2 Corinthians 8:1–5"},"). He does not order the Corinthians to match them. He sets their gift beside the grace of Christ, who \"though He was rich, yet for your sakes He became poor\" (",{"r":"2CO.8.8-11","t":"2 Corinthians 8:8–11"},")."]},{"k":"p","runs":["The measure is what a person has, not what they lack, and the aim is not to relieve some by burdening others (",{"r":"2CO.8.12-14","t":"2 Corinthians 8:12–14"},"). Then Paul quotes the story of the manna, where he who gathered much had no excess and he who gathered little had no shortfall (",{"r":"2CO.8.15","t":"2 Corinthians 8:15"},", quoting ",{"r":"EXO.16.18","t":"Exodus 16:18"},")."]},{"k":"quote","t":"Each one should give what he has decided in his heart to give, not out of regret or compulsion. For God loves a cheerful giver.","r":"2CO.9.7","label":"2 Corinthians 9:7"},{"k":"care","runs":["Paul's language of sowing and reaping is sometimes taught as a rate of financial return. Follow the sentences to where they actually go: God will \"increase the harvest of your righteousness\", you will be enriched \"to be generous on every occasion\", and the result is \"thanksgiving to God\" (",{"r":"2CO.9.10-12","t":"2 Corinthians 9:10–12"},"). Along the way he quotes ",{"r":"PSA.112.9","t":"Psalm 112:9"}," on the one who has \"scattered abroad His gifts to the poor\" (",{"r":"2CO.9.9","t":"2 Corinthians 9:9"},"). The harvest here is more generosity and more thanks, not private wealth. The confession speaks of stewardship: giving \"cheerfully, regularly, systematically, proportionately, and liberally\" (Article 13). It does not promise riches as a reward for faith, and neither does this passage."]}]},{"title":"Where confidence rests","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["First Timothy joins godliness with contentment and warns of what the desire to be rich does to people (",{"r":"1TI.6.6-10","t":"1 Timothy 6:6–10"},"). It then turns to those who already have wealth: do not be conceited, do not hope in uncertain riches but in God, do good, and be \"generous and ready to share\" (",{"r":"1TI.6.17-19","t":"1 Timothy 6:17–19"},"). Put in this site's words: contentment asks what you truly need, and generosity asks what you could give. The two belong together."]}]}],"slug":"money","hook":["The poorest churches begged for the privilege of giving."],"line":["Giving is measured by what you have, and aimed at someone's real need."],"read":["2CO.8.1-15","2CO.9.6-15","1TI.6.6-19"],"says":["Give willingly, according to what you have; be content; if you are rich, do not trust in riches, and be generous and ready to share."],"setting":["A collection for needy believers, with the Macedonian churches giving out of deep poverty. First Timothy addresses both people who want to be rich and people who already are."],"respond":["Find one real need and decide what you can responsibly share."],"look":["How does Paul connect willingness with a person's means? What results of giving does he name beyond the gift itself?"],"response":["Identify a real need and what you can responsibly share. Keep that person's good in view, not your own display or any bargain for later gain."],"verseCount":39},{"n":"04","title":"Hospitality","parts":[{"title":"Making room for others","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["Romans sets hospitality among the marks of sincere love and meeting the needs of the saints (",{"r":"ROM.12.9-13","t":"Romans 12:9–13"},"). Hebrews puts welcoming strangers beside brotherly love and remembering prisoners \"as if you were bound with them\" (",{"r":"HEB.13.1-3","t":"Hebrews 13:1–3"},"). It adds that some \"have entertained angels without knowing it\" and does not say who; a reader may think of Abraham's visitors in ",{"r":"GEN.18.1-8","t":"Genesis 18:1–8"},", though Hebrews does not name them."]},{"k":"p","runs":["None of these passages describes an impressive house or an elaborate meal. Their concern is the person welcomed. A simple meal, a place in the conversation or some practical help can all express it. Those examples are this site's, not a list from the text."]}]},{"title":"Without complaining","blocks":[{"k":"quote","t":"Show hospitality to one another without complaining.","r":"1PE.4.9","label":"1 Peter 4:9"},{"k":"p","runs":["First Peter sets hospitality among love and service. Whatever you have received is for serving others, as a steward of God's grace, in the strength God provides, so that in all things God may be glorified (",{"r":"1PE.4.8-11","t":"1 Peter 4:8–11"},"). So attention moves away from the host. This site's application: a welcome that humiliates the guest, or keeps reminding them what it cost, has missed the point."]}]}],"slug":"table","hook":["Some guests were more than they seemed."],"line":["Making room for people who might otherwise be overlooked, and doing it without complaint."],"read":["ROM.12.9-13","HEB.13.1-3","1PE.4.8-11"],"says":["Practise hospitality, do not neglect strangers, remember prisoners and the mistreated, and serve one another without complaining."],"setting":["Sincere love among believers; strangers and sufferers; each person's gifts used as a steward of God's grace."],"respond":["Think of one person who needs a welcome, and offer something modest that you can give willingly."],"look":["Who receives particular attention in Hebrews? How does First Peter connect hospitality with other kinds of service?"],"response":["Think of someone who could use a welcome or practical care. Choose something modest and specific that you can offer willingly."],"verseCount":12},{"n":"05","title":"Neighbours and authorities","parts":[{"title":"Peace and the good of a neighbour","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["Romans tells you to bless those who persecute you, to weep with those who weep, and never to repay evil for evil. \"If it is possible on your part, live at peace with everyone\" (",{"r":"ROM.12.14-18","t":"Romans 12:14–18"},"). That qualification matters: you answer for your own conduct, and you cannot control every response. Revenge is ruled out because it is God's, and Paul quotes ",{"r":"DEU.32.35","t":"Deuteronomy 32:35"}," to say so. Then he quotes ",{"r":"PRO.25.21-22","t":"Proverbs 25:21–22"},": feed your enemy if he is hungry (",{"r":"ROM.12.19-21","t":"Romans 12:19–21"},")."]},{"k":"p","runs":["After speaking of public authorities, Paul comes back to the neighbour. He lists commandments from ",{"r":"EXO.20.13-17","t":"Exodus 20:13–17"}," and gathers them under ",{"r":"LEV.19.18","t":"Leviticus 19:18"},": \"Love your neighbor as yourself\" (",{"r":"ROM.13.8-10","t":"Romans 13:8–10"},"). Love here has moral content. It is more than a friendly manner."]}]},{"title":"Authority under God","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["Romans 13 tells everyone to submit to the governing authorities, says they are appointed by God, and calls for paying taxes and giving honour where they are due (",{"r":"ROM.13.1-7","t":"Romans 13:1–7"},"). First Peter says the same \"for the Lord's sake\" (",{"r":"1PE.2.13-17","t":"1 Peter 2:13–17"},")."]},{"k":"quote","t":"Treat everyone with high regard: Love the brotherhood of believers, fear God, honor the king.","r":"1PE.2.17","label":"1 Peter 2:17"},{"k":"p","runs":["Notice the two verbs in that verse: God is feared, and the king is honoured. In Acts, ordered to stop teaching in Jesus' name, the apostles answer, \"We must obey God rather than men\" (",{"r":"ACT.5.27-29","t":"Acts 5:27–29"},"). That is one particular clash over their witness, not a general permission to ignore duties we dislike. The confession says the same in brief: Christians owe the state obedience in what is not \"contrary to the revealed will of God\", and \"God alone is Lord of the conscience\" (Article 17)."]},{"k":"open","runs":["A further question stays open. When a government commands nothing against God but rules unjustly, how far may a Christian resist? Calvin, the Reformed commentator, on Romans 13, says that rulers often fall short of their duty, \"yet the obedience due to princes ought to be rendered to them\". Gill, the Baptist, in his Body of Practical Divinity, says rulers are obeyed in what is \"not contrary to the laws of God, and the fundamental laws of the kingdom\". The confession sets one limit, God's revealed will, and is silent beyond it. This study does not choose, and it names no present government."]}]}],"slug":"street","hook":["Your enemy is hungry. What do you owe him?"],"line":["Peace, taxes, honour and love for your neighbour, all under a God who is greater than any ruler."],"read":["ROM.12.14-13.10","1PE.2.11-17","ACT.5.27-29"],"says":["Bless persecutors; do not take revenge; submit to the governing authorities and pay what you owe; love your neighbour."],"setting":["Believers living under Roman rule, some of them slandered. Acts, a narrative rather than a letter, records one particular clash between a human order and God's command."],"respond":["Take one public responsibility and one person affected by how you carry it out, and ask what honesty and honour require."],"look":["How does love of neighbour frame what Paul says about public duties? What is the difference between fearing God and honouring a ruler?"],"response":["Take one public responsibility and one nearby person affected by your conduct. What would honesty, honour and care for their good ask of you?"],"verseCount":28},{"n":"06","title":"Conscience and disputed matters","parts":[{"title":"Receiving without contempt","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["Romans describes believers who differ over food and over special days. Those who eat must not belittle those who abstain, and those who abstain must not judge those who eat, because each answers to the Lord (",{"r":"ROM.14.1-12","t":"Romans 14:1–12"},"). Paul quotes ",{"r":"ISA.45.23","t":"Isaiah 45:23"}," to make the point: every knee will bow, and each of us will give an account (",{"r":"ROM.14.11-12","t":"Romans 14:11–12"},")."]},{"k":"p","runs":["This is about the practices it names. It does not make every action a matter of taste. Paul has just named conduct that wrongs a neighbour (",{"r":"ROM.13.8-10","t":"Romans 13:8–10"},"), so the call to welcome is no refusal to tell good from evil."]}]},{"title":"Freedom attentive to another person","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":["The question becomes bigger than \"may I?\" Does what you do put a stumbling block in someone's way? Does it serve peace and build them up (",{"r":"ROM.14.13-23","t":"Romans 14:13–23"},")? The strong are to bear with the weak and not please themselves, because even Christ did not please himself. Paul quotes ",{"r":"PSA.69.9","t":"Psalm 69:9"}," there, and ends with a reason to carry away: accept one another \"just as Christ accepted you\" (",{"r":"ROM.15.1-7","t":"Romans 15:1–7"},")."]},{"k":"p","runs":["First Corinthians gives a sharp example. Someone with a weak conscience sees you eating in an idol's temple and is encouraged to do what he believes is wrong. Paul calls him \"this weak brother, for whom Christ died\" (",{"r":"1CO.8.9-13","t":"1 Corinthians 8:9–13"},"). This is more serious than annoying someone. Another person is being drawn into what they believe is unfaithful."]},{"k":"p","runs":["A conscience should not be bullied into acting, and yet a conviction can be taught. The confession's line \"God alone is Lord of the conscience\" (Article 17) is written about church and state, but its point holds here too. Go back to the passage, listen carefully, and seek the other person's good without contempt."]}]}],"slug":"conscience","hook":["One plate of meat. One brother for whom Christ died."],"line":["Where believers differ over food and days, welcome each other and watch what your freedom does to someone else."],"read":["ROM.14.1-15.7","1CO.8.1-13"],"says":["Accept one another without contempt or judgment; do not put a stumbling block in a brother's way; the strong are to bear with the weak."],"setting":["Disputes over food and special days in Rome, and over food offered to idols in Corinth. These are the matters named, not every possible disagreement."],"respond":["In a disputed practice, separate your preference, your conviction and the effect on someone else."],"look":["What differences does Romans actually discuss? In First Corinthians, how could one person's freedom harm another?"],"response":["In a disputed practice, separate your preference, your conviction and the possible effect on someone else. Would restraint, a patient conversation or further study serve them better?"],"verseCount":43}],"title":"Faith in daily life","concepts":["Home · Work · Money · Table · Street · Conscience"],"motto":["A door. A bench. A bowl. / Each one before the Lord."],"lead":["The letters were written to people with spouses, children, masters, debts, guests and neighbours. They do not only say what to do. Read closely, and the sentence often tells you why: because of the Lord, or for the good of the person in front of you. This study walks six everyday places and teaches you to ask each instruction that one question."],"opening":{"k":"quote","t":"Love does no wrong to its neighbor. Therefore love is the fulfillment of the law.","r":"ROM.13.10","label":"Romans 13:10"},"frame":["These passages were sent to real communities. Some of their settings are like yours; others, above all slavery, are not, and must not be quietly treated as if they were. So begin with what the passage said to the people who first heard it. Only then ask what faithfulness looks like in the responsibility before you."],"selection":["This is a selection, not a census. These six places were chosen because the letters return to each of them and because together they cover home, work, possessions, guests, public life and disputes between believers. Other lists differ: the household instructions also appear in ",{"r":"TIT.2.1-10","t":"Titus 2:1–10"}," and ",{"r":"1PE.2.18-3.7","t":"1 Peter 2:18–3:7"},", which this study does not walk, and illness, old age, widowhood and unpaid care have no reading of their own here."],"closing":"Faithfulness in what is before us","way":["Ask the sentence why. In any instruction you read: who is being spoken to, what are they asked to do, what reason does the sentence give, and what carries over to you and what does not?"],"close":["Love takes form in patient care, honest work, generosity, welcome and attention to a neighbour. You do not have to begin with all six. Begin with the one already in front of you."],"question":["Which one responsibility in front of you this week would change, if you did it as to the Lord and for the good of the person beside you?"],"again":["Read the passage again before you answer."],"passage":"COL.3.23-24"},"passages":{"ROM.13.10":{"label":"Romans 13:10","code":"ROM","chapters":[13],"verses":[{"c":13,"v":10,"t":"Love does no wrong to its neighbor. Therefore love is the fulfillment of the law."}]},"TIT.2.1-10":{"label":"Titus 2:1–10","code":"TIT","chapters":[2],"verses":[{"c":2,"v":1,"t":"But as for you, speak the things that are consistent with sound doctrine."},{"c":2,"v":2,"t":"Older men are to be temperate, dignified, self-controlled, and sound in faith, love, and perseverance."},{"c":2,"v":3,"t":"Older women, likewise, are to be reverent in their behavior, not slanderers or addicted to much wine, but teachers of good."},{"c":2,"v":4,"t":"In this way they can train the young women to love their husbands and children,"},{"c":2,"v":5,"t":"to be self-controlled, pure, managers of their households, kind, and submissive to their own husbands, so that the word of God will not be discredited."},{"c":2,"v":6,"t":"In the same way, urge the younger men to be self-controlled."},{"c":2,"v":7,"t":"In everything, show yourself to be an example by doing good works. In your teaching show integrity, dignity,"},{"c":2,"v":8,"t":"and wholesome speech that is above reproach, so that anyone who opposes us will be ashamed to have nothing bad to say about us."},{"c":2,"v":9,"t":"Slaves are to submit to their own masters in everything, to be well-pleasing, not argumentative,"},{"c":2,"v":10,"t":"not stealing from them, but showing all good faith, so that in every respect they will adorn the teaching about God our Savior."}]},"1PE.2.18-3.7":{"label":"1 Peter 2:18–3:7","code":"1PE","chapters":[2,3],"verses":[{"c":2,"v":18,"t":"Servants, submit yourselves to your masters with all respect, not only to those who are good and gentle, but even to those who are unreasonable."},{"c":2,"v":19,"t":"For if anyone endures the pain of unjust suffering because he is conscious of God, this is to be commended."},{"c":2,"v":20,"t":"How is it to your credit if you are beaten for doing wrong and you endure it? But if you suffer for doing good and you endure it, this is commendable before God."},{"c":2,"v":21,"t":"For to this you were called, because Christ also suffered for you, leaving you an example, that you should follow in His footsteps:"},{"c":2,"v":22,"t":"“He committed no sin, and no deceit was found in His mouth.”"},{"c":2,"v":23,"t":"When they heaped abuse on Him, He did not retaliate; when He suffered, He made no threats, but entrusted Himself to Him who judges justly."},{"c":2,"v":24,"t":"He Himself bore our sins in His body on the tree, so that we might die to sin and live to righteousness. “By His stripes you are healed.”"},{"c":2,"v":25,"t":"For “you were like sheep going astray,” but now you have returned to the Shepherd and Overseer of your souls."},{"c":3,"v":1,"t":"Wives, in the same way, submit yourselves to your husbands, so that even if they refuse to believe the word, they will be won over without words by the behavior of their wives"},{"c":3,"v":2,"t":"when they see your pure and reverent demeanor."},{"c":3,"v":3,"t":"Your beauty should not come from outward adornment, such as braided hair or gold jewelry or fine clothes,"},{"c":3,"v":4,"t":"but from the inner disposition of your heart, the unfading beauty of a gentle and quiet spirit, which is precious in God’s sight."},{"c":3,"v":5,"t":"For this is how the holy women of the past adorned themselves. They put their hope in God and were submissive to their husbands,"},{"c":3,"v":6,"t":"just as Sarah obeyed Abraham and called him lord. And you are her children if you do what is right and refuse to give way to fear."},{"c":3,"v":7,"t":"Husbands, in the same way, treat your wives with consideration as a delicate vessel, and with honor as fellow heirs of the gracious gift of life, so that your prayers will not be hindered."}]},"EPH.5.21-6.4":{"label":"Ephesians 5:21–6:4","code":"EPH","chapters":[5,6],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":21,"t":"Submit to one another out of reverence for Christ."},{"c":5,"v":22,"t":"Wives, submit to your husbands as to the Lord."},{"c":5,"v":23,"t":"For the husband is the head of the wife as Christ is the head of the church, His body, of which He is the Savior."},{"c":5,"v":24,"t":"Now as the church submits to Christ, so also wives should submit to their husbands in everything."},{"c":5,"v":25,"t":"Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ loved the church and gave Himself up for her"},{"c":5,"v":26,"t":"to sanctify her, cleansing her by the washing with water through the word,"},{"c":5,"v":27,"t":"and to present her to Himself as a glorious church, without stain or wrinkle or any such blemish, but holy and blameless."},{"c":5,"v":28,"t":"In the same way, husbands ought to love their wives as their own bodies. He who loves his wife loves himself."},{"c":5,"v":29,"t":"Indeed, no one ever hated his own body, but he nourishes and cherishes it, just as Christ does the church."},{"c":5,"v":30,"t":"For we are members of His body."},{"c":5,"v":31,"t":"“For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and the two will become one flesh.”"},{"c":5,"v":32,"t":"This mystery is profound, but I am speaking about Christ and the church."},{"c":5,"v":33,"t":"Nevertheless, each one of you also must love his wife as he loves himself, and the wife must respect her husband."},{"c":6,"v":1,"t":"Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this is right."},{"c":6,"v":2,"t":"“Honor your father and mother” (which is the first commandment with a promise),"},{"c":6,"v":3,"t":"“that it may go well with you and that you may have a long life on the earth.”"},{"c":6,"v":4,"t":"Fathers, do not provoke your children to wrath; instead, bring them up in the discipline and instruction of the Lord."}]},"COL.3.18-21":{"label":"Colossians 3:18–21","code":"COL","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":18,"t":"Wives, submit to your husbands, as is fitting in the Lord."},{"c":3,"v":19,"t":"Husbands, love your wives and do not be harsh with them."},{"c":3,"v":20,"t":"Children, obey your parents in everything, for this is pleasing to the Lord."},{"c":3,"v":21,"t":"Fathers, do not provoke your children, so they will not become discouraged."}]},"COL.4.16":{"label":"Colossians 4:16","code":"COL","chapters":[4],"verses":[{"c":4,"v":16,"t":"After this letter has been read among you, make sure that it is also read in the church of the Laodiceans, and that you in turn read the letter from Laodicea."}]},"EPH.5.21":{"label":"Ephesians 5:21","code":"EPH","chapters":[5],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":21,"t":"Submit to one another out of reverence for Christ."}]},"EPH.5.22-33":{"label":"Ephesians 5:22–33","code":"EPH","chapters":[5],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":22,"t":"Wives, submit to your husbands as to the Lord."},{"c":5,"v":23,"t":"For the husband is the head of the wife as Christ is the head of the church, His body, of which He is the Savior."},{"c":5,"v":24,"t":"Now as the church submits to Christ, so also wives should submit to their husbands in everything."},{"c":5,"v":25,"t":"Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ loved the church and gave Himself up for her"},{"c":5,"v":26,"t":"to sanctify her, cleansing her by the washing with water through the word,"},{"c":5,"v":27,"t":"and to present her to Himself as a glorious church, without stain or wrinkle or any such blemish, but holy and blameless."},{"c":5,"v":28,"t":"In the same way, husbands ought to love their wives as their own bodies. He who loves his wife loves himself."},{"c":5,"v":29,"t":"Indeed, no one ever hated his own body, but he nourishes and cherishes it, just as Christ does the church."},{"c":5,"v":30,"t":"For we are members of His body."},{"c":5,"v":31,"t":"“For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and the two will become one flesh.”"},{"c":5,"v":32,"t":"This mystery is profound, but I am speaking about Christ and the church."},{"c":5,"v":33,"t":"Nevertheless, each one of you also must love his wife as he loves himself, and the wife must respect her husband."}]},"EPH.5.25":{"label":"Ephesians 5:25","code":"EPH","chapters":[5],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":25,"t":"Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ loved the church and gave Himself up for her"}]},"GEN.2.24":{"label":"Genesis 2:24","code":"GEN","chapters":[2],"verses":[{"c":2,"v":24,"t":"For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and they will become one flesh."}]},"EPH.5.31-32":{"label":"Ephesians 5:31–32","code":"EPH","chapters":[5],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":31,"t":"“For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and the two will become one flesh.”"},{"c":5,"v":32,"t":"This mystery is profound, but I am speaking about Christ and the church."}]},"COL.3.18-19":{"label":"Colossians 3:18–19","code":"COL","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":18,"t":"Wives, submit to your husbands, as is fitting in the Lord."},{"c":3,"v":19,"t":"Husbands, love your wives and do not be harsh with them."}]},"COL.3.19":{"label":"Colossians 3:19","code":"COL","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":19,"t":"Husbands, love your wives and do not be harsh with them."}]},"EPH.6.1-3":{"label":"Ephesians 6:1–3","code":"EPH","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":1,"t":"Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this is right."},{"c":6,"v":2,"t":"“Honor your father and mother” (which is the first commandment with a promise),"},{"c":6,"v":3,"t":"“that it may go well with you and that you may have a long life on the earth.”"}]},"EXO.20.12":{"label":"Exodus 20:12","code":"EXO","chapters":[20],"verses":[{"c":20,"v":12,"t":"Honor your father and mother, so that your days may be long in the land that the LORD your God is giving you."}]},"EPH.6.4":{"label":"Ephesians 6:4","code":"EPH","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":4,"t":"Fathers, do not provoke your children to wrath; instead, bring them up in the discipline and instruction of the Lord."}]},"COL.3.20-21":{"label":"Colossians 3:20–21","code":"COL","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":20,"t":"Children, obey your parents in everything, for this is pleasing to the Lord."},{"c":3,"v":21,"t":"Fathers, do not provoke your children, so they will not become discouraged."}]},"1CO.7.7-8":{"label":"1 Corinthians 7:7–8","code":"1CO","chapters":[7],"verses":[{"c":7,"v":7,"t":"I wish that all men were as I am. But each man has his own gift from God; one has this gift, another has that."},{"c":7,"v":8,"t":"Now to the unmarried and widows I say this: It is good for them to remain unmarried, as I am."}]},"EPH.4.28":{"label":"Ephesians 4:28","code":"EPH","chapters":[4],"verses":[{"c":4,"v":28,"t":"He who has been stealing must steal no longer, but must work, doing good with his own hands, that he may have something to share with the one in need."}]},"1TH.4.9-12":{"label":"1 Thessalonians 4:9–12","code":"1TH","chapters":[4],"verses":[{"c":4,"v":9,"t":"Now about brotherly love, you do not need anyone to write to you, because you yourselves have been taught by God to love one another."},{"c":4,"v":10,"t":"And you are indeed showing this love to all the brothers throughout Macedonia. But we urge you, brothers, to excel more and more"},{"c":4,"v":11,"t":"and to aspire to live quietly, to attend to your own matters, and to work with your own hands, as we instructed you."},{"c":4,"v":12,"t":"Then you will behave properly toward outsiders, without being dependent on anyone."}]},"2TH.3.6-15":{"label":"2 Thessalonians 3:6–15","code":"2TH","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":6,"t":"Now we command you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to keep away from any brother who leads an undisciplined life that is not in keeping with the tradition you received from us."},{"c":3,"v":7,"t":"For you yourselves know how you ought to imitate us, because we were not undisciplined among you,"},{"c":3,"v":8,"t":"nor did we eat anyone’s food without paying for it. Instead, in labor and toil, we worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to any of you."},{"c":3,"v":9,"t":"Not that we lack this right, but we wanted to offer ourselves as an example for you to imitate."},{"c":3,"v":10,"t":"For even while we were with you, we gave you this command: “If anyone is unwilling to work, he shall not eat.”"},{"c":3,"v":11,"t":"Yet we hear that some of you are leading undisciplined lives and accomplishing nothing but being busybodies."},{"c":3,"v":12,"t":"We command and urge such people by our Lord Jesus Christ to begin working quietly to earn their own living."},{"c":3,"v":13,"t":"But as for you, brothers, do not grow weary in well-doing."},{"c":3,"v":14,"t":"Take note of anyone who does not obey the instructions we have given in this letter. Do not associate with him, so that he may be ashamed."},{"c":3,"v":15,"t":"Yet do not regard him as an enemy, but warn him as a brother."}]},"EPH.6.5-9":{"label":"Ephesians 6:5–9","code":"EPH","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":5,"t":"Slaves, obey your earthly masters with respect and fear and sincerity of heart, just as you would obey Christ."},{"c":6,"v":6,"t":"And do this not only to please them while they are watching, but as servants of Christ, doing the will of God from your heart."},{"c":6,"v":7,"t":"Serve with good will, as to the Lord and not to men,"},{"c":6,"v":8,"t":"because you know that the Lord will reward each one for whatever good he does, whether he is slave or free."},{"c":6,"v":9,"t":"And masters, do the same for your slaves. Give up your use of threats, because you know that He who is both their Master and yours is in heaven, and there is no favoritism with Him."}]},"COL.3.22-4.1":{"label":"Colossians 3:22–4:1","code":"COL","chapters":[3,4],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":22,"t":"Slaves, obey your earthly masters in everything, not only to please them while they are watching, but with sincerity of heart and fear of the Lord."},{"c":3,"v":23,"t":"Whatever you do, work at it with your whole being, for the Lord and not for men,"},{"c":3,"v":24,"t":"because you know that you will receive an inheritance from the Lord as your reward. It is the Lord Christ you are serving."},{"c":3,"v":25,"t":"Whoever does wrong will be repaid for his wrong, and there is no favoritism."},{"c":4,"v":1,"t":"Masters, supply your slaves with what is right and fair, since you know that you also have a Master in heaven."}]},"2TH.3.6-12":{"label":"2 Thessalonians 3:6–12","code":"2TH","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":6,"t":"Now we command you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to keep away from any brother who leads an undisciplined life that is not in keeping with the tradition you received from us."},{"c":3,"v":7,"t":"For you yourselves know how you ought to imitate us, because we were not undisciplined among you,"},{"c":3,"v":8,"t":"nor did we eat anyone’s food without paying for it. Instead, in labor and toil, we worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to any of you."},{"c":3,"v":9,"t":"Not that we lack this right, but we wanted to offer ourselves as an example for you to imitate."},{"c":3,"v":10,"t":"For even while we were with you, we gave you this command: “If anyone is unwilling to work, he shall not eat.”"},{"c":3,"v":11,"t":"Yet we hear that some of you are leading undisciplined lives and accomplishing nothing but being busybodies."},{"c":3,"v":12,"t":"We command and urge such people by our Lord Jesus Christ to begin working quietly to earn their own living."}]},"2TH.3.13-15":{"label":"2 Thessalonians 3:13–15","code":"2TH","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":13,"t":"But as for you, brothers, do not grow weary in well-doing."},{"c":3,"v":14,"t":"Take note of anyone who does not obey the instructions we have given in this letter. Do not associate with him, so that he may be ashamed."},{"c":3,"v":15,"t":"Yet do not regard him as an enemy, but warn him as a brother."}]},"EPH.6.8":{"label":"Ephesians 6:8","code":"EPH","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":8,"t":"because you know that the Lord will reward each one for whatever good he does, whether he is slave or free."}]},"1TI.1.10":{"label":"1 Timothy 1:10","code":"1TI","chapters":[1],"verses":[{"c":1,"v":10,"t":"for the sexually immoral, for homosexuals, for slave traders and liars and perjurers, and for anyone else who is averse to sound teaching"}]},"PHM.1.16":{"label":"Philemon 1:16","code":"PHM","chapters":[1],"verses":[{"c":1,"v":16,"t":"no longer as a slave, but better than a slave, as a beloved brother. He is especially beloved to me, but even more so to you, both in person and in the Lord."}]},"2CO.8.1-15":{"label":"2 Corinthians 8:1–15","code":"2CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":1,"t":"Now, brothers, we want you to know about the grace that God has given the churches of Macedonia."},{"c":8,"v":2,"t":"In the terrible ordeal they suffered, their abundant joy and deep poverty overflowed into rich generosity."},{"c":8,"v":3,"t":"For I testify that they gave according to their ability and even beyond it. Of their own accord,"},{"c":8,"v":4,"t":"they earnestly pleaded with us for the privilege of sharing in this service to the saints."},{"c":8,"v":5,"t":"And not only did they do as we expected, but they gave themselves first to the Lord and then to us, because it was the will of God."},{"c":8,"v":6,"t":"So we urged Titus to help complete your act of grace, just as he had started it."},{"c":8,"v":7,"t":"But just as you excel in everything—in faith, in speech, in knowledge, in complete earnestness, and in the love we inspired in you —see that you also excel in this grace of giving."},{"c":8,"v":8,"t":"I am not making a demand, but I am testing the sincerity of your love in comparison to the earnestness of others."},{"c":8,"v":9,"t":"For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that though He was rich, yet for your sakes He became poor, so that you through His poverty might become rich."},{"c":8,"v":10,"t":"And this is my opinion about what is helpful for you in this matter: Last year you were the first not only to give, but even to have such a desire."},{"c":8,"v":11,"t":"Now finish the work, so that you may complete it just as eagerly as you began, according to your means."},{"c":8,"v":12,"t":"For if the eagerness is there, the gift is acceptable according to what one has, not according to what he does not have."},{"c":8,"v":13,"t":"It is not our intention that others may be relieved while you are burdened, but that there may be equality."},{"c":8,"v":14,"t":"At the present time, your surplus will meet their need, so that in turn their surplus will meet your need. Then there will be equality."},{"c":8,"v":15,"t":"As it is written: “He who gathered much had no excess, and he who gathered little had no shortfall.”"}]},"2CO.9.6-15":{"label":"2 Corinthians 9:6–15","code":"2CO","chapters":[9],"verses":[{"c":9,"v":6,"t":"Remember this: Whoever sows sparingly will also reap sparingly, and whoever sows generously will also reap generously."},{"c":9,"v":7,"t":"Each one should give what he has decided in his heart to give, not out of regret or compulsion. For God loves a cheerful giver."},{"c":9,"v":8,"t":"And God is able to make all grace abound to you, so that in all things, at all times, having all that you need, you will abound in every good work."},{"c":9,"v":9,"t":"As it is written: “He has scattered abroad His gifts to the poor; His righteousness endures forever.”"},{"c":9,"v":10,"t":"Now He who supplies seed to the sower and bread for food will supply and multiply your store of seed and will increase the harvest of your righteousness."},{"c":9,"v":11,"t":"You will be enriched in every way to be generous on every occasion, so that through us your giving will produce thanksgiving to God."},{"c":9,"v":12,"t":"For this ministry of service is not only supplying the needs of the saints, but is also overflowing in many expressions of thanksgiving to God."},{"c":9,"v":13,"t":"Because of the proof this ministry provides, the saints will glorify God for your obedient confession of the gospel of Christ, and for the generosity of your contribution to them and to all the others."},{"c":9,"v":14,"t":"And their prayers for you will express their affection for you, because of the surpassing grace God has given you."},{"c":9,"v":15,"t":"Thanks be to God for His indescribable gift!"}]},"1TI.6.6-19":{"label":"1 Timothy 6:6–19","code":"1TI","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":6,"t":"Of course, godliness with contentment is great gain."},{"c":6,"v":7,"t":"For we brought nothing into the world, so we cannot carry anything out of it."},{"c":6,"v":8,"t":"But if we have food and clothing, we will be content with these."},{"c":6,"v":9,"t":"Those who want to be rich, however, fall into temptation and become ensnared by many foolish and harmful desires that plunge them into ruin and destruction."},{"c":6,"v":10,"t":"For the love of money is the root of all kinds of evil. By craving it, some have wandered away from the faith and pierced themselves with many sorrows."},{"c":6,"v":11,"t":"But you, O man of God, flee from these things and pursue righteousness, godliness, faith, love, perseverance, and gentleness."},{"c":6,"v":12,"t":"Fight the good fight of the faith. Take hold of the eternal life to which you were called when you made the good confession before many witnesses."},{"c":6,"v":13,"t":"I charge you in the presence of God, who gives life to all things, and of Christ Jesus, who made the good confession in His testimony before Pontius Pilate:"},{"c":6,"v":14,"t":"Keep this commandment without stain or reproach until the appearance of our Lord Jesus Christ,"},{"c":6,"v":15,"t":"which the blessed and only Sovereign One—the King of kings and Lord of lords—will bring about in His own time."},{"c":6,"v":16,"t":"He alone is immortal and dwells in unapproachable light. No one has ever seen Him, nor can anyone see Him. To Him be honor and eternal dominion! Amen."},{"c":6,"v":17,"t":"Instruct those who are rich in the present age not to be conceited and not to put their hope in the uncertainty of wealth, but in God, who richly provides all things for us to enjoy."},{"c":6,"v":18,"t":"Instruct them to do good, to be rich in good works, and to be generous and ready to share,"},{"c":6,"v":19,"t":"treasuring up for themselves a firm foundation for the future, so that they may take hold of that which is truly life."}]},"2CO.8.1-5":{"label":"2 Corinthians 8:1–5","code":"2CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":1,"t":"Now, brothers, we want you to know about the grace that God has given the churches of Macedonia."},{"c":8,"v":2,"t":"In the terrible ordeal they suffered, their abundant joy and deep poverty overflowed into rich generosity."},{"c":8,"v":3,"t":"For I testify that they gave according to their ability and even beyond it. Of their own accord,"},{"c":8,"v":4,"t":"they earnestly pleaded with us for the privilege of sharing in this service to the saints."},{"c":8,"v":5,"t":"And not only did they do as we expected, but they gave themselves first to the Lord and then to us, because it was the will of God."}]},"2CO.8.8-11":{"label":"2 Corinthians 8:8–11","code":"2CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":8,"t":"I am not making a demand, but I am testing the sincerity of your love in comparison to the earnestness of others."},{"c":8,"v":9,"t":"For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that though He was rich, yet for your sakes He became poor, so that you through His poverty might become rich."},{"c":8,"v":10,"t":"And this is my opinion about what is helpful for you in this matter: Last year you were the first not only to give, but even to have such a desire."},{"c":8,"v":11,"t":"Now finish the work, so that you may complete it just as eagerly as you began, according to your means."}]},"2CO.8.12-14":{"label":"2 Corinthians 8:12–14","code":"2CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":12,"t":"For if the eagerness is there, the gift is acceptable according to what one has, not according to what he does not have."},{"c":8,"v":13,"t":"It is not our intention that others may be relieved while you are burdened, but that there may be equality."},{"c":8,"v":14,"t":"At the present time, your surplus will meet their need, so that in turn their surplus will meet your need. Then there will be equality."}]},"2CO.8.15":{"label":"2 Corinthians 8:15","code":"2CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":15,"t":"As it is written: “He who gathered much had no excess, and he who gathered little had no shortfall.”"}]},"EXO.16.18":{"label":"Exodus 16:18","code":"EXO","chapters":[16],"verses":[{"c":16,"v":18,"t":"When they measured it by the omer, he who gathered much had no excess, and he who gathered little had no shortfall. Each one gathered as much as he needed to eat."}]},"2CO.9.7":{"label":"2 Corinthians 9:7","code":"2CO","chapters":[9],"verses":[{"c":9,"v":7,"t":"Each one should give what he has decided in his heart to give, not out of regret or compulsion. For God loves a cheerful giver."}]},"2CO.9.10-12":{"label":"2 Corinthians 9:10–12","code":"2CO","chapters":[9],"verses":[{"c":9,"v":10,"t":"Now He who supplies seed to the sower and bread for food will supply and multiply your store of seed and will increase the harvest of your righteousness."},{"c":9,"v":11,"t":"You will be enriched in every way to be generous on every occasion, so that through us your giving will produce thanksgiving to God."},{"c":9,"v":12,"t":"For this ministry of service is not only supplying the needs of the saints, but is also overflowing in many expressions of thanksgiving to God."}]},"PSA.112.9":{"label":"Psalm 112:9","code":"PSA","chapters":[112],"verses":[{"c":112,"v":9,"t":"He has scattered abroad his gifts to the poor; his righteousness endures forever; his horn will be lifted high in honor."}]},"2CO.9.9":{"label":"2 Corinthians 9:9","code":"2CO","chapters":[9],"verses":[{"c":9,"v":9,"t":"As it is written: “He has scattered abroad His gifts to the poor; His righteousness endures forever.”"}]},"1TI.6.6-10":{"label":"1 Timothy 6:6–10","code":"1TI","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":6,"t":"Of course, godliness with contentment is great gain."},{"c":6,"v":7,"t":"For we brought nothing into the world, so we cannot carry anything out of it."},{"c":6,"v":8,"t":"But if we have food and clothing, we will be content with these."},{"c":6,"v":9,"t":"Those who want to be rich, however, fall into temptation and become ensnared by many foolish and harmful desires that plunge them into ruin and destruction."},{"c":6,"v":10,"t":"For the love of money is the root of all kinds of evil. By craving it, some have wandered away from the faith and pierced themselves with many sorrows."}]},"1TI.6.17-19":{"label":"1 Timothy 6:17–19","code":"1TI","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":17,"t":"Instruct those who are rich in the present age not to be conceited and not to put their hope in the uncertainty of wealth, but in God, who richly provides all things for us to enjoy."},{"c":6,"v":18,"t":"Instruct them to do good, to be rich in good works, and to be generous and ready to share,"},{"c":6,"v":19,"t":"treasuring up for themselves a firm foundation for the future, so that they may take hold of that which is truly life."}]},"ROM.12.9-13":{"label":"Romans 12:9–13","code":"ROM","chapters":[12],"verses":[{"c":12,"v":9,"t":"Love must be sincere. Detest what is evil; cling to what is good."},{"c":12,"v":10,"t":"Be devoted to one another in brotherly love. Outdo yourselves in honoring one another."},{"c":12,"v":11,"t":"Do not let your zeal subside; keep your spiritual fervor, serving the Lord."},{"c":12,"v":12,"t":"Be joyful in hope, patient in affliction, persistent in prayer."},{"c":12,"v":13,"t":"Share with the saints who are in need. Practice hospitality."}]},"HEB.13.1-3":{"label":"Hebrews 13:1–3","code":"HEB","chapters":[13],"verses":[{"c":13,"v":1,"t":"Continue in brotherly love."},{"c":13,"v":2,"t":"Do not neglect to show hospitality to strangers, for by so doing some people have entertained angels without knowing it."},{"c":13,"v":3,"t":"Remember those in prison as if you were bound with them, and those who are mistreated as if you were suffering with them."}]},"1PE.4.8-11":{"label":"1 Peter 4:8–11","code":"1PE","chapters":[4],"verses":[{"c":4,"v":8,"t":"Above all, love one another deeply, because love covers over a multitude of sins."},{"c":4,"v":9,"t":"Show hospitality to one another without complaining."},{"c":4,"v":10,"t":"As good stewards of the manifold grace of God, each of you should use whatever gift he has received to serve one another."},{"c":4,"v":11,"t":"If anyone speaks, he should speak as one conveying the words of God. If anyone serves, he should serve with the strength God provides, so that in all things God may be glorified through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory and the power forever and ever. Amen."}]},"GEN.18.1-8":{"label":"Genesis 18:1–8","code":"GEN","chapters":[18],"verses":[{"c":18,"v":1,"t":"Then the LORD appeared to Abraham by the Oaks of Mamre in the heat of the day, while he was sitting at the entrance of his tent."},{"c":18,"v":2,"t":"And Abraham looked up and saw three men standing nearby. When he saw them, he ran from the entrance of his tent to meet them and bowed low to the ground."},{"c":18,"v":3,"t":"“My lord,” said Abraham, “if I have found favor in your sight, please do not pass your servant by."},{"c":18,"v":4,"t":"Let a little water be brought, that you may wash your feet and rest yourselves under the tree."},{"c":18,"v":5,"t":"And I will bring a bit of bread so that you may refresh yourselves. This is why you have passed your servant’s way. After that, you may continue on your way.” “Yes,” they replied, “you may do as you have said.”"},{"c":18,"v":6,"t":"So Abraham hurried into the tent and said to Sarah, “Quick! Prepare three seahs of fine flour, knead it, and bake some bread.”"},{"c":18,"v":7,"t":"Meanwhile, Abraham ran to the herd, selected a tender and choice calf, and gave it to a servant, who hurried to prepare it."},{"c":18,"v":8,"t":"Then Abraham brought curds and milk and the calf that had been prepared, and he set them before the men and stood by them under the tree as they ate."}]},"1PE.4.9":{"label":"1 Peter 4:9","code":"1PE","chapters":[4],"verses":[{"c":4,"v":9,"t":"Show hospitality to one another without complaining."}]},"ROM.12.14-13.10":{"label":"Romans 12:14–13:10","code":"ROM","chapters":[12,13],"verses":[{"c":12,"v":14,"t":"Bless those who persecute you. Bless and do not curse."},{"c":12,"v":15,"t":"Rejoice with those who rejoice; weep with those who weep."},{"c":12,"v":16,"t":"Live in harmony with one another. Do not be proud, but enjoy the company of the lowly. Do not be conceited."},{"c":12,"v":17,"t":"Do not repay anyone evil for evil. Carefully consider what is right in the eyes of everybody."},{"c":12,"v":18,"t":"If it is possible on your part, live at peace with everyone."},{"c":12,"v":19,"t":"Do not avenge yourselves, beloved, but leave room for God’s wrath. For it is written: “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay, says the Lord.”"},{"c":12,"v":20,"t":"On the contrary, “If your enemy is hungry, feed him; if he is thirsty, give him a drink. For in so doing, you will heap burning coals on his head.”"},{"c":12,"v":21,"t":"Do not be overcome by evil, but overcome evil with good."},{"c":13,"v":1,"t":"Everyone must submit himself to the governing authorities, for there is no authority except that which is from God. The authorities that exist have been appointed by God."},{"c":13,"v":2,"t":"Consequently, whoever resists authority is opposing what God has set in place, and those who do so will bring judgment on themselves."},{"c":13,"v":3,"t":"For rulers are not a terror to good conduct, but to bad. Do you want to be unafraid of the one in authority? Then do what is right, and you will have his approval."},{"c":13,"v":4,"t":"For he is God’s servant for your good. But if you do wrong, be afraid, for he does not carry the sword in vain. He is God’s servant, an agent of retribution to the wrongdoer."},{"c":13,"v":5,"t":"Therefore it is necessary to submit to authority, not only to avoid punishment, but also as a matter of conscience."},{"c":13,"v":6,"t":"This is also why you pay taxes. For the authorities are God’s servants, who devote themselves to their work."},{"c":13,"v":7,"t":"Pay everyone what you owe him: taxes to whom taxes are due, revenue to whom revenue is due, respect to whom respect is due, honor to whom honor is due."},{"c":13,"v":8,"t":"Be indebted to no one, except to one another in love. For he who loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law."},{"c":13,"v":9,"t":"The commandments “Do not commit adultery,” “Do not murder,” “Do not steal,” “Do not covet,” and any other commandments, are summed up in this one decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.”"},{"c":13,"v":10,"t":"Love does no wrong to its neighbor. Therefore love is the fulfillment of the law."}]},"1PE.2.11-17":{"label":"1 Peter 2:11–17","code":"1PE","chapters":[2],"verses":[{"c":2,"v":11,"t":"Beloved, I urge you, as foreigners and exiles, to abstain from the desires of the flesh, which war against your soul."},{"c":2,"v":12,"t":"Conduct yourselves with such honor among the Gentiles that, though they slander you as evildoers, they may see your good deeds and glorify God on the day He visits us."},{"c":2,"v":13,"t":"Submit yourselves for the Lord’s sake to every human institution, whether to the king as the supreme authority,"},{"c":2,"v":14,"t":"or to governors as those sent by him to punish those who do wrong and to praise those who do right."},{"c":2,"v":15,"t":"For it is God’s will that by doing good you should silence the ignorance of foolish men."},{"c":2,"v":16,"t":"Live in freedom, but do not use your freedom as a cover-up for evil; live as servants of God."},{"c":2,"v":17,"t":"Treat everyone with high regard: Love the brotherhood of believers, fear God, honor the king."}]},"ACT.5.27-29":{"label":"Acts 5:27–29","code":"ACT","chapters":[5],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":27,"t":"They brought them in and made them stand before the Sanhedrin, where the high priest interrogated them."},{"c":5,"v":28,"t":"“We gave you strict orders not to teach in this name,” he said. “Yet you have filled Jerusalem with your teaching and are determined to make us responsible for this man’s blood.”"},{"c":5,"v":29,"t":"But Peter and the other apostles replied, “We must obey God rather than men."}]},"ROM.12.14-18":{"label":"Romans 12:14–18","code":"ROM","chapters":[12],"verses":[{"c":12,"v":14,"t":"Bless those who persecute you. Bless and do not curse."},{"c":12,"v":15,"t":"Rejoice with those who rejoice; weep with those who weep."},{"c":12,"v":16,"t":"Live in harmony with one another. Do not be proud, but enjoy the company of the lowly. Do not be conceited."},{"c":12,"v":17,"t":"Do not repay anyone evil for evil. Carefully consider what is right in the eyes of everybody."},{"c":12,"v":18,"t":"If it is possible on your part, live at peace with everyone."}]},"DEU.32.35":{"label":"Deuteronomy 32:35","code":"DEU","chapters":[32],"verses":[{"c":32,"v":35,"t":"Vengeance is Mine; I will repay. In due time their foot will slip; for their day of disaster is near, and their doom is coming quickly.”"}]},"PRO.25.21-22":{"label":"Proverbs 25:21–22","code":"PRO","chapters":[25],"verses":[{"c":25,"v":21,"t":"If your enemy is hungry, give him food to eat, and if he is thirsty, give him water to drink."},{"c":25,"v":22,"t":"For in so doing, you will heap burning coals on his head, and the LORD will reward you."}]},"ROM.12.19-21":{"label":"Romans 12:19–21","code":"ROM","chapters":[12],"verses":[{"c":12,"v":19,"t":"Do not avenge yourselves, beloved, but leave room for God’s wrath. For it is written: “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay, says the Lord.”"},{"c":12,"v":20,"t":"On the contrary, “If your enemy is hungry, feed him; if he is thirsty, give him a drink. For in so doing, you will heap burning coals on his head.”"},{"c":12,"v":21,"t":"Do not be overcome by evil, but overcome evil with good."}]},"EXO.20.13-17":{"label":"Exodus 20:13–17","code":"EXO","chapters":[20],"verses":[{"c":20,"v":13,"t":"You shall not murder."},{"c":20,"v":14,"t":"You shall not commit adultery."},{"c":20,"v":15,"t":"You shall not steal."},{"c":20,"v":16,"t":"You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor."},{"c":20,"v":17,"t":"You shall not covet your neighbor’s house. You shall not covet your neighbor’s wife, or his manservant or maidservant, or his ox or donkey, or anything that belongs to your neighbor.”"}]},"LEV.19.18":{"label":"Leviticus 19:18","code":"LEV","chapters":[19],"verses":[{"c":19,"v":18,"t":"Do not seek revenge or bear a grudge against any of your people, but love your neighbor as yourself. I am the LORD."}]},"ROM.13.8-10":{"label":"Romans 13:8–10","code":"ROM","chapters":[13],"verses":[{"c":13,"v":8,"t":"Be indebted to no one, except to one another in love. For he who loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law."},{"c":13,"v":9,"t":"The commandments “Do not commit adultery,” “Do not murder,” “Do not steal,” “Do not covet,” and any other commandments, are summed up in this one decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.”"},{"c":13,"v":10,"t":"Love does no wrong to its neighbor. Therefore love is the fulfillment of the law."}]},"ROM.13.1-7":{"label":"Romans 13:1–7","code":"ROM","chapters":[13],"verses":[{"c":13,"v":1,"t":"Everyone must submit himself to the governing authorities, for there is no authority except that which is from God. The authorities that exist have been appointed by God."},{"c":13,"v":2,"t":"Consequently, whoever resists authority is opposing what God has set in place, and those who do so will bring judgment on themselves."},{"c":13,"v":3,"t":"For rulers are not a terror to good conduct, but to bad. Do you want to be unafraid of the one in authority? Then do what is right, and you will have his approval."},{"c":13,"v":4,"t":"For he is God’s servant for your good. But if you do wrong, be afraid, for he does not carry the sword in vain. He is God’s servant, an agent of retribution to the wrongdoer."},{"c":13,"v":5,"t":"Therefore it is necessary to submit to authority, not only to avoid punishment, but also as a matter of conscience."},{"c":13,"v":6,"t":"This is also why you pay taxes. For the authorities are God’s servants, who devote themselves to their work."},{"c":13,"v":7,"t":"Pay everyone what you owe him: taxes to whom taxes are due, revenue to whom revenue is due, respect to whom respect is due, honor to whom honor is due."}]},"1PE.2.13-17":{"label":"1 Peter 2:13–17","code":"1PE","chapters":[2],"verses":[{"c":2,"v":13,"t":"Submit yourselves for the Lord’s sake to every human institution, whether to the king as the supreme authority,"},{"c":2,"v":14,"t":"or to governors as those sent by him to punish those who do wrong and to praise those who do right."},{"c":2,"v":15,"t":"For it is God’s will that by doing good you should silence the ignorance of foolish men."},{"c":2,"v":16,"t":"Live in freedom, but do not use your freedom as a cover-up for evil; live as servants of God."},{"c":2,"v":17,"t":"Treat everyone with high regard: Love the brotherhood of believers, fear God, honor the king."}]},"1PE.2.17":{"label":"1 Peter 2:17","code":"1PE","chapters":[2],"verses":[{"c":2,"v":17,"t":"Treat everyone with high regard: Love the brotherhood of believers, fear God, honor the king."}]},"ROM.14.1-15.7":{"label":"Romans 14:1–15:7","code":"ROM","chapters":[14,15],"verses":[{"c":14,"v":1,"t":"Accept him whose faith is weak, without passing judgment on his opinions."},{"c":14,"v":2,"t":"For one person has faith to eat all things, while another, who is weak, eats only vegetables."},{"c":14,"v":3,"t":"The one who eats everything must not belittle the one who does not, and the one who does not eat everything must not judge the one who does, for God has accepted him."},{"c":14,"v":4,"t":"Who are you to judge someone else’s servant? To his own master he stands or falls. And he will stand, for the Lord is able to make him stand."},{"c":14,"v":5,"t":"One person regards a certain day above the others, while someone else considers every day alike. Each one should be fully convinced in his own mind."},{"c":14,"v":6,"t":"He who observes a special day does so to the Lord; he who eats does so to the Lord, for he gives thanks to God; and he who abstains does so to the Lord and gives thanks to God."},{"c":14,"v":7,"t":"For none of us lives to himself alone, and none of us dies to himself alone."},{"c":14,"v":8,"t":"If we live, we live to the Lord, and if we die, we die to the Lord. So whether we live or die, we belong to the Lord."},{"c":14,"v":9,"t":"For this reason Christ died and returned to life, that He might be the Lord of both the dead and the living."},{"c":14,"v":10,"t":"Why, then, do you judge your brother? Or why do you belittle your brother? For we will all stand before God’s judgment seat."},{"c":14,"v":11,"t":"It is written: “As surely as I live, says the Lord, every knee will bow before Me; every tongue will confess to God.”"},{"c":14,"v":12,"t":"So then, each of us will give an account of himself to God."},{"c":14,"v":13,"t":"Therefore let us stop judging one another. Instead, make up your mind not to put any stumbling block or obstacle in your brother’s way."},{"c":14,"v":14,"t":"I am convinced and fully persuaded in the Lord Jesus that nothing is unclean in itself. But if anyone regards something as unclean, then for him it is unclean."},{"c":14,"v":15,"t":"If your brother is distressed by what you eat, you are no longer acting in love. Do not by your eating destroy your brother, for whom Christ died."},{"c":14,"v":16,"t":"Do not allow what you consider good, then, to be spoken of as evil."},{"c":14,"v":17,"t":"For the kingdom of God is not a matter of eating and drinking, but of righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit."},{"c":14,"v":18,"t":"For whoever serves Christ in this way is pleasing to God and approved by men."},{"c":14,"v":19,"t":"So then, let us pursue what leads to peace and to mutual edification."},{"c":14,"v":20,"t":"Do not destroy the work of God for the sake of food. All food is clean, but it is wrong for a man to let his eating be a stumbling block."},{"c":14,"v":21,"t":"It is better not to eat meat or drink wine or to do anything to cause your brother to stumble."},{"c":14,"v":22,"t":"Keep your belief about such matters between yourself and God. Blessed is the one who does not condemn himself by what he approves."},{"c":14,"v":23,"t":"But the one who has doubts is condemned if he eats, because his eating is not from faith; and everything that is not from faith is sin."},{"c":15,"v":1,"t":"We who are strong ought to bear with the shortcomings of the weak and not to please ourselves."},{"c":15,"v":2,"t":"Each of us should please his neighbor for his good, to build him up."},{"c":15,"v":3,"t":"For even Christ did not please Himself, but as it is written: “The insults of those who insult You have fallen on Me.”"},{"c":15,"v":4,"t":"For everything that was written in the past was written for our instruction, so that through endurance and the encouragement of the Scriptures, we might have hope."},{"c":15,"v":5,"t":"Now may the God who gives endurance and encouragement grant you harmony with one another in Christ Jesus,"},{"c":15,"v":6,"t":"so that with one mind and one voice you may glorify the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ."},{"c":15,"v":7,"t":"Accept one another, then, just as Christ accepted you, in order to bring glory to God."}]},"1CO.8.1-13":{"label":"1 Corinthians 8:1–13","code":"1CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":1,"t":"Now about food sacrificed to idols: We know that we all have knowledge. Knowledge puffs up, but love builds up."},{"c":8,"v":2,"t":"The one who thinks he knows something does not yet know as he ought to know."},{"c":8,"v":3,"t":"But the one who loves God is known by God."},{"c":8,"v":4,"t":"So about eating food sacrificed to idols: We know that an idol is nothing at all in the world, and that there is no God but one."},{"c":8,"v":5,"t":"For even if there are so-called gods, whether in heaven or on earth (as there are many so-called gods and lords),"},{"c":8,"v":6,"t":"yet for us there is but one God, the Father, from whom all things came and for whom we exist. And there is but one Lord, Jesus Christ, through whom all things came and through whom we exist."},{"c":8,"v":7,"t":"But not everyone has this knowledge. Some people are still so accustomed to idols that they eat such food as if it were sacrificed to an idol. And since their conscience is weak, it is defiled."},{"c":8,"v":8,"t":"But food does not bring us closer to God: We are no worse if we do not eat, and no better if we do."},{"c":8,"v":9,"t":"Be careful, however, that your freedom does not become a stumbling block to the weak."},{"c":8,"v":10,"t":"For if someone with a weak conscience sees you who are well informed eating in an idol’s temple, will he not be encouraged to eat food sacrificed to idols?"},{"c":8,"v":11,"t":"So this weak brother, for whom Christ died, is destroyed by your knowledge."},{"c":8,"v":12,"t":"By sinning against your brothers in this way and wounding their weak conscience, you sin against Christ."},{"c":8,"v":13,"t":"Therefore, if what I eat causes my brother to stumble, I will never eat meat again, so that I will not cause him to stumble."}]},"ROM.14.1-12":{"label":"Romans 14:1–12","code":"ROM","chapters":[14],"verses":[{"c":14,"v":1,"t":"Accept him whose faith is weak, without passing judgment on his opinions."},{"c":14,"v":2,"t":"For one person has faith to eat all things, while another, who is weak, eats only vegetables."},{"c":14,"v":3,"t":"The one who eats everything must not belittle the one who does not, and the one who does not eat everything must not judge the one who does, for God has accepted him."},{"c":14,"v":4,"t":"Who are you to judge someone else’s servant? To his own master he stands or falls. And he will stand, for the Lord is able to make him stand."},{"c":14,"v":5,"t":"One person regards a certain day above the others, while someone else considers every day alike. Each one should be fully convinced in his own mind."},{"c":14,"v":6,"t":"He who observes a special day does so to the Lord; he who eats does so to the Lord, for he gives thanks to God; and he who abstains does so to the Lord and gives thanks to God."},{"c":14,"v":7,"t":"For none of us lives to himself alone, and none of us dies to himself alone."},{"c":14,"v":8,"t":"If we live, we live to the Lord, and if we die, we die to the Lord. So whether we live or die, we belong to the Lord."},{"c":14,"v":9,"t":"For this reason Christ died and returned to life, that He might be the Lord of both the dead and the living."},{"c":14,"v":10,"t":"Why, then, do you judge your brother? Or why do you belittle your brother? For we will all stand before God’s judgment seat."},{"c":14,"v":11,"t":"It is written: “As surely as I live, says the Lord, every knee will bow before Me; every tongue will confess to God.”"},{"c":14,"v":12,"t":"So then, each of us will give an account of himself to God."}]},"ISA.45.23":{"label":"Isaiah 45:23","code":"ISA","chapters":[45],"verses":[{"c":45,"v":23,"t":"By Myself I have sworn; truth has gone out from My mouth, a word that will not be revoked: Every knee will bow before Me, every tongue will swear allegiance."}]},"ROM.14.11-12":{"label":"Romans 14:11–12","code":"ROM","chapters":[14],"verses":[{"c":14,"v":11,"t":"It is written: “As surely as I live, says the Lord, every knee will bow before Me; every tongue will confess to God.”"},{"c":14,"v":12,"t":"So then, each of us will give an account of himself to God."}]},"ROM.14.13-23":{"label":"Romans 14:13–23","code":"ROM","chapters":[14],"verses":[{"c":14,"v":13,"t":"Therefore let us stop judging one another. Instead, make up your mind not to put any stumbling block or obstacle in your brother’s way."},{"c":14,"v":14,"t":"I am convinced and fully persuaded in the Lord Jesus that nothing is unclean in itself. But if anyone regards something as unclean, then for him it is unclean."},{"c":14,"v":15,"t":"If your brother is distressed by what you eat, you are no longer acting in love. Do not by your eating destroy your brother, for whom Christ died."},{"c":14,"v":16,"t":"Do not allow what you consider good, then, to be spoken of as evil."},{"c":14,"v":17,"t":"For the kingdom of God is not a matter of eating and drinking, but of righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit."},{"c":14,"v":18,"t":"For whoever serves Christ in this way is pleasing to God and approved by men."},{"c":14,"v":19,"t":"So then, let us pursue what leads to peace and to mutual edification."},{"c":14,"v":20,"t":"Do not destroy the work of God for the sake of food. All food is clean, but it is wrong for a man to let his eating be a stumbling block."},{"c":14,"v":21,"t":"It is better not to eat meat or drink wine or to do anything to cause your brother to stumble."},{"c":14,"v":22,"t":"Keep your belief about such matters between yourself and God. Blessed is the one who does not condemn himself by what he approves."},{"c":14,"v":23,"t":"But the one who has doubts is condemned if he eats, because his eating is not from faith; and everything that is not from faith is sin."}]},"PSA.69.9":{"label":"Psalm 69:9","code":"PSA","chapters":[69],"verses":[{"c":69,"v":9,"t":"because zeal for Your house has consumed me, and the insults of those who insult You have fallen on me."}]},"ROM.15.1-7":{"label":"Romans 15:1–7","code":"ROM","chapters":[15],"verses":[{"c":15,"v":1,"t":"We who are strong ought to bear with the shortcomings of the weak and not to please ourselves."},{"c":15,"v":2,"t":"Each of us should please his neighbor for his good, to build him up."},{"c":15,"v":3,"t":"For even Christ did not please Himself, but as it is written: “The insults of those who insult You have fallen on Me.”"},{"c":15,"v":4,"t":"For everything that was written in the past was written for our instruction, so that through endurance and the encouragement of the Scriptures, we might have hope."},{"c":15,"v":5,"t":"Now may the God who gives endurance and encouragement grant you harmony with one another in Christ Jesus,"},{"c":15,"v":6,"t":"so that with one mind and one voice you may glorify the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ."},{"c":15,"v":7,"t":"Accept one another, then, just as Christ accepted you, in order to bring glory to God."}]},"1CO.8.9-13":{"label":"1 Corinthians 8:9–13","code":"1CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":9,"t":"Be careful, however, that your freedom does not become a stumbling block to the weak."},{"c":8,"v":10,"t":"For if someone with a weak conscience sees you who are well informed eating in an idol’s temple, will he not be encouraged to eat food sacrificed to idols?"},{"c":8,"v":11,"t":"So this weak brother, for whom Christ died, is destroyed by your knowledge."},{"c":8,"v":12,"t":"By sinning against your brothers in this way and wounding their weak conscience, you sin against Christ."},{"c":8,"v":13,"t":"Therefore, if what I eat causes my brother to stumble, I will never eat meat again, so that I will not cause him to stumble."}]},"COL.3.23-24":{"label":"Colossians 3:23–24","code":"COL","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":23,"t":"Whatever you do, work at it with your whole being, for the Lord and not for men,"},{"c":3,"v":24,"t":"because you know that you will receive an inheritance from the Lord as your reward. It is the Lord Christ you are serving."}]},"EPH.5.22":{"label":"Ephesians 5:22","code":"EPH","chapters":[5],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":22,"t":"Wives, submit to your husbands as to the Lord."}]},"EPH.6.1":{"label":"Ephesians 6:1","code":"EPH","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":1,"t":"Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this is right."}]},"COL.3.20":{"label":"Colossians 3:20","code":"COL","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":20,"t":"Children, obey your parents in everything, for this is pleasing to the Lord."}]},"EPH.5.28":{"label":"Ephesians 5:28","code":"EPH","chapters":[5],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":28,"t":"In the same way, husbands ought to love their wives as their own bodies. He who loves his wife loves himself."}]},"COL.3.21":{"label":"Colossians 3:21","code":"COL","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":21,"t":"Fathers, do not provoke your children, so they will not become discouraged."}]},"EPH.6.7":{"label":"Ephesians 6:7","code":"EPH","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":7,"t":"Serve with good will, as to the Lord and not to men,"}]},"EPH.6.9":{"label":"Ephesians 6:9","code":"EPH","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":9,"t":"And masters, do the same for your slaves. Give up your use of threats, because you know that He who is both their Master and yours is in heaven, and there is no favoritism with Him."}]},"COL.3.24":{"label":"Colossians 3:24","code":"COL","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":24,"t":"because you know that you will receive an inheritance from the Lord as your reward. It is the Lord Christ you are serving."}]},"1TH.4.12":{"label":"1 Thessalonians 4:12","code":"1TH","chapters":[4],"verses":[{"c":4,"v":12,"t":"Then you will behave properly toward outsiders, without being dependent on anyone."}]},"2TH.3.8":{"label":"2 Thessalonians 3:8","code":"2TH","chapters":[3],"verses":[{"c":3,"v":8,"t":"nor did we eat anyone’s food without paying for it. Instead, in labor and toil, we worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to any of you."}]},"2CO.8.9":{"label":"2 Corinthians 8:9","code":"2CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":9,"t":"For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that though He was rich, yet for your sakes He became poor, so that you through His poverty might become rich."}]},"2CO.9.11":{"label":"2 Corinthians 9:11","code":"2CO","chapters":[9],"verses":[{"c":9,"v":11,"t":"You will be enriched in every way to be generous on every occasion, so that through us your giving will produce thanksgiving to God."}]},"1TI.6.17":{"label":"1 Timothy 6:17","code":"1TI","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":17,"t":"Instruct those who are rich in the present age not to be conceited and not to put their hope in the uncertainty of wealth, but in God, who richly provides all things for us to enjoy."}]},"2CO.8.14":{"label":"2 Corinthians 8:14","code":"2CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":14,"t":"At the present time, your surplus will meet their need, so that in turn their surplus will meet your need. Then there will be equality."}]},"2CO.9.12":{"label":"2 Corinthians 9:12","code":"2CO","chapters":[9],"verses":[{"c":9,"v":12,"t":"For this ministry of service is not only supplying the needs of the saints, but is also overflowing in many expressions of thanksgiving to God."}]},"1PE.4.10":{"label":"1 Peter 4:10","code":"1PE","chapters":[4],"verses":[{"c":4,"v":10,"t":"As good stewards of the manifold grace of God, each of you should use whatever gift he has received to serve one another."}]},"1PE.4.11":{"label":"1 Peter 4:11","code":"1PE","chapters":[4],"verses":[{"c":4,"v":11,"t":"If anyone speaks, he should speak as one conveying the words of God. If anyone serves, he should serve with the strength God provides, so that in all things God may be glorified through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory and the power forever and ever. Amen."}]},"HEB.13.3":{"label":"Hebrews 13:3","code":"HEB","chapters":[13],"verses":[{"c":13,"v":3,"t":"Remember those in prison as if you were bound with them, and those who are mistreated as if you were suffering with them."}]},"ROM.12.19":{"label":"Romans 12:19","code":"ROM","chapters":[12],"verses":[{"c":12,"v":19,"t":"Do not avenge yourselves, beloved, but leave room for God’s wrath. For it is written: “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay, says the Lord.”"}]},"ROM.13.1":{"label":"Romans 13:1","code":"ROM","chapters":[13],"verses":[{"c":13,"v":1,"t":"Everyone must submit himself to the governing authorities, for there is no authority except that which is from God. The authorities that exist have been appointed by God."}]},"1PE.2.13":{"label":"1 Peter 2:13","code":"1PE","chapters":[2],"verses":[{"c":2,"v":13,"t":"Submit yourselves for the Lord’s sake to every human institution, whether to the king as the supreme authority,"}]},"ACT.5.29":{"label":"Acts 5:29","code":"ACT","chapters":[5],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":29,"t":"But Peter and the other apostles replied, “We must obey God rather than men."}]},"ROM.13.8":{"label":"Romans 13:8","code":"ROM","chapters":[13],"verses":[{"c":13,"v":8,"t":"Be indebted to no one, except to one another in love. For he who loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law."}]},"ROM.14.3":{"label":"Romans 14:3","code":"ROM","chapters":[14],"verses":[{"c":14,"v":3,"t":"The one who eats everything must not belittle the one who does not, and the one who does not eat everything must not judge the one who does, for God has accepted him."}]},"ROM.14.8":{"label":"Romans 14:8","code":"ROM","chapters":[14],"verses":[{"c":14,"v":8,"t":"If we live, we live to the Lord, and if we die, we die to the Lord. So whether we live or die, we belong to the Lord."}]},"ROM.15.7":{"label":"Romans 15:7","code":"ROM","chapters":[15],"verses":[{"c":15,"v":7,"t":"Accept one another, then, just as Christ accepted you, in order to bring glory to God."}]},"1CO.8.12":{"label":"1 Corinthians 8:12","code":"1CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":12,"t":"By sinning against your brothers in this way and wounding their weak conscience, you sin against Christ."}]},"ROM.14.13":{"label":"Romans 14:13","code":"ROM","chapters":[14],"verses":[{"c":14,"v":13,"t":"Therefore let us stop judging one another. Instead, make up your mind not to put any stumbling block or obstacle in your brother’s way."}]},"ROM.15.2":{"label":"Romans 15:2","code":"ROM","chapters":[15],"verses":[{"c":15,"v":2,"t":"Each of us should please his neighbor for his good, to build him up."}]},"1CO.8.13":{"label":"1 Corinthians 8:13","code":"1CO","chapters":[8],"verses":[{"c":8,"v":13,"t":"Therefore, if what I eat causes my brother to stumble, I will never eat meat again, so that I will not cause him to stumble."}]},"EPH.5.31":{"label":"Ephesians 5:31","code":"EPH","chapters":[5],"verses":[{"c":5,"v":31,"t":"“For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and the two will become one flesh.”"}]},"EPH.6.2":{"label":"Ephesians 6:2","code":"EPH","chapters":[6],"verses":[{"c":6,"v":2,"t":"“Honor your father and mother” (which is the first commandment with a promise),"}]},"ROM.12.20":{"label":"Romans 12:20","code":"ROM","chapters":[12],"verses":[{"c":12,"v":20,"t":"On the contrary, “If your enemy is hungry, feed him; if he is thirsty, give him a drink. For in so doing, you will heap burning coals on his head.”"}]},"ROM.13.9":{"label":"Romans 13:9","code":"ROM","chapters":[13],"verses":[{"c":13,"v":9,"t":"The commandments “Do not commit adultery,” “Do not murder,” “Do not steal,” “Do not covet,” and any other commandments, are summed up in this one decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.”"}]},"ROM.14.11":{"label":"Romans 14:11","code":"ROM","chapters":[14],"verses":[{"c":14,"v":11,"t":"It is written: “As surely as I live, says the Lord, every knee will bow before Me; every tongue will confess to God.”"}]},"ROM.15.3":{"label":"Romans 15:3","code":"ROM","chapters":[15],"verses":[{"c":15,"v":3,"t":"For even Christ did not please Himself, but as it is written: “The insults of those who insult You have fallen on Me.”"}]}},"reasons":[{"place":"home","r":"EPH.5.22","label":"Ephesians 5:22","pole":"L","pre":"Wives, submit to your husbands ","mark":"as to the Lord","post":"."},{"place":"home","r":"EPH.5.25","label":"Ephesians 5:25","pole":"L","pre":"Husbands, love your wives, ","mark":"just as Christ loved the church","post":" and gave Himself up for her"},{"place":"home","r":"EPH.6.1","label":"Ephesians 6:1","pole":"L","pre":"Children, obey your parents ","mark":"in the Lord","post":", for this is right."},{"place":"home","r":"COL.3.20","label":"Colossians 3:20","pole":"L","pre":"Children, obey your parents in everything, for this is ","mark":"pleasing to the Lord","post":"."},{"place":"home","r":"EPH.5.28","label":"Ephesians 5:28","pole":"N","pre":"In the same way, husbands ought to love their wives ","mark":"as their own bodies","post":". He who loves his wife loves himself."},{"place":"home","r":"COL.3.21","label":"Colossians 3:21","pole":"N","pre":"Fathers, do not provoke your children, ","mark":"so they will not become discouraged","post":"."},{"place":"work","r":"EPH.6.7","label":"Ephesians 6:7","pole":"L","pre":"Serve with good will, ","mark":"as to the Lord and not to men","post":","},{"place":"work","r":"EPH.6.9","label":"Ephesians 6:9","pole":"L","pre":"And masters, do the same for your slaves. Give up your use of threats, because you know that ","mark":"He who is both their Master and yours is in heaven","post":", and there is no favoritism with Him."},{"place":"work","r":"COL.3.24","label":"Colossians 3:24","pole":"L","pre":"because you know that you will receive an inheritance from the Lord as your reward. ","mark":"It is the Lord Christ you are serving","post":"."},{"place":"work","r":"EPH.4.28","label":"Ephesians 4:28","pole":"N","pre":"He who has been stealing must steal no longer, but must work, doing good with his own hands, that he may have ","mark":"something to share with the one in need","post":"."},{"place":"work","r":"1TH.4.12","label":"1 Thessalonians 4:12","pole":"N","pre":"Then you will ","mark":"behave properly toward outsiders","post":", without being dependent on anyone."},{"place":"work","r":"2TH.3.8","label":"2 Thessalonians 3:8","pole":"N","pre":"nor did we eat anyone’s food without paying for it. Instead, in labor and toil, we worked night and day ","mark":"so that we would not be a burden","post":" to any of you."},{"place":"money","r":"2CO.8.9","label":"2 Corinthians 8:9","pole":"L","pre":"For you know ","mark":"the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ","post":", that though He was rich, yet for your sakes He became poor, so that you through His poverty might become rich."},{"place":"money","r":"2CO.9.7","label":"2 Corinthians 9:7","pole":"L","pre":"Each one should give what he has decided in his heart to give, not out of regret or compulsion. For ","mark":"God loves a cheerful giver","post":"."},{"place":"money","r":"2CO.9.11","label":"2 Corinthians 9:11","pole":"L","pre":"You will be enriched in every way to be generous on every occasion, so that through us your giving will produce ","mark":"thanksgiving to God","post":"."},{"place":"money","r":"1TI.6.17","label":"1 Timothy 6:17","pole":"L","pre":"Instruct those who are rich in the present age not to be conceited and not to put their hope in the uncertainty of wealth, but ","mark":"in God, who richly provides","post":" all things for us to enjoy."},{"place":"money","r":"2CO.8.14","label":"2 Corinthians 8:14","pole":"N","pre":"At the present time, ","mark":"your surplus will meet their need","post":", so that in turn their surplus will meet your need. Then there will be equality."},{"place":"money","r":"2CO.9.12","label":"2 Corinthians 9:12","pole":"N","pre":"For this ministry of service is not only ","mark":"supplying the needs of the saints","post":", but is also overflowing in many expressions of thanksgiving to God."},{"place":"table","r":"1PE.4.10","label":"1 Peter 4:10","pole":"L","pre":"As ","mark":"good stewards of the manifold grace of God","post":", each of you should use whatever gift he has received to serve one another."},{"place":"table","r":"1PE.4.11","label":"1 Peter 4:11","pole":"L","pre":"If anyone speaks, he should speak as one conveying the words of God. If anyone serves, he should serve with the strength God provides, ","mark":"so that in all things God may be glorified","post":" through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory and the power forever and ever. Amen."},{"place":"table","r":"HEB.13.3","label":"Hebrews 13:3","pole":"N","pre":"Remember those in prison ","mark":"as if you were bound with them","post":", and those who are mistreated as if you were suffering with them."},{"place":"table","r":"1PE.4.10","label":"1 Peter 4:10","pole":"N","pre":"As good stewards of the manifold grace of God, each of you should use whatever gift he has received ","mark":"to serve one another","post":"."},{"place":"street","r":"ROM.12.19","label":"Romans 12:19","pole":"L","pre":"Do not avenge yourselves, beloved, but ","mark":"leave room for God’s wrath","post":". For it is written: “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay, says the Lord.”"},{"place":"street","r":"ROM.13.1","label":"Romans 13:1","pole":"L","pre":"Everyone must submit himself to the governing authorities, for there is no authority except that which is from God. The authorities that exist have been ","mark":"appointed by God","post":"."},{"place":"street","r":"1PE.2.13","label":"1 Peter 2:13","pole":"L","pre":"Submit yourselves ","mark":"for the Lord’s sake","post":" to every human institution, whether to the king as the supreme authority,"},{"place":"street","r":"ACT.5.29","label":"Acts 5:29","pole":"L","pre":"But Peter and the other apostles replied, “We must ","mark":"obey God rather than men","post":"."},{"place":"street","r":"ROM.13.8","label":"Romans 13:8","pole":"N","pre":"Be indebted to no one, except to one another in love. For ","mark":"he who loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law","post":"."},{"place":"street","r":"ROM.13.10","label":"Romans 13:10","pole":"N","pre":"","mark":"Love does no wrong to its neighbor","post":". Therefore love is the fulfillment of the law."},{"place":"conscience","r":"ROM.14.3","label":"Romans 14:3","pole":"L","pre":"The one who eats everything must not belittle the one who does not, and the one who does not eat everything must not judge the one who does, ","mark":"for God has accepted him","post":"."},{"place":"conscience","r":"ROM.14.8","label":"Romans 14:8","pole":"L","pre":"If we live, we live to the Lord, and if we die, we die to the Lord. So whether we live or die, ","mark":"we belong to the Lord","post":"."},{"place":"conscience","r":"ROM.15.7","label":"Romans 15:7","pole":"L","pre":"Accept one another, then, ","mark":"just as Christ accepted you","post":", in order to bring glory to God."},{"place":"conscience","r":"1CO.8.12","label":"1 Corinthians 8:12","pole":"L","pre":"By sinning against your brothers in this way and wounding their weak conscience, ","mark":"you sin against Christ","post":"."},{"place":"conscience","r":"ROM.14.13","label":"Romans 14:13","pole":"N","pre":"Therefore let us stop judging one another. Instead, make up your mind not to put ","mark":"any stumbling block or obstacle","post":" in your brother’s way."},{"place":"conscience","r":"ROM.15.2","label":"Romans 15:2","pole":"N","pre":"Each of us should ","mark":"please his neighbor for his good","post":", to build him up."},{"place":"conscience","r":"1CO.8.13","label":"1 Corinthians 8:13","pole":"N","pre":"Therefore, if what I eat causes my brother to stumble, I will never eat meat again, ","mark":"so that I will not cause him to stumble","post":"."}],"pairs":[{"id":"pair-1","older":"GEN.2.24","olderLabel":"Genesis 2:24","letter":"EPH.5.31","letterLabel":"Ephesians 5:31","section":"history","sectionName":"History"},{"id":"pair-2","older":"EXO.20.12","olderLabel":"Exodus 20:12","letter":"EPH.6.2","letterLabel":"Ephesians 6:2","section":"history","sectionName":"History"},{"id":"pair-3","older":"EXO.16.18","olderLabel":"Exodus 16:18","letter":"2CO.8.15","letterLabel":"2 Corinthians 8:15","section":"history","sectionName":"History"},{"id":"pair-4","older":"PSA.112.9","olderLabel":"Psalm 112:9","letter":"2CO.9.9","letterLabel":"2 Corinthians 9:9","section":"poetry","sectionName":"Poetry & Wisdom"},{"id":"pair-5","older":"DEU.32.35","olderLabel":"Deuteronomy 32:35","letter":"ROM.12.19","letterLabel":"Romans 12:19","section":"history","sectionName":"History"},{"id":"pair-6","older":"PRO.25.21-22","olderLabel":"Proverbs 25:21–22","letter":"ROM.12.20","letterLabel":"Romans 12:20","section":"poetry","sectionName":"Poetry & Wisdom"},{"id":"pair-7","older":"EXO.20.13-17","olderLabel":"Exodus 20:13–17","letter":"ROM.13.9","letterLabel":"Romans 13:9","section":"history","sectionName":"History"},{"id":"pair-8","older":"LEV.19.18","olderLabel":"Leviticus 19:18","letter":"ROM.13.9","letterLabel":"Romans 13:9","section":"history","sectionName":"History"},{"id":"pair-9","older":"ISA.45.23","olderLabel":"Isaiah 45:23","letter":"ROM.14.11","letterLabel":"Romans 14:11","section":"prophets","sectionName":"Prophets"},{"id":"pair-10","older":"PSA.69.9","olderLabel":"Psalm 69:9","letter":"ROM.15.3","letterLabel":"Romans 15:3","section":"poetry","sectionName":"Poetry & Wisdom"}],"sources":[{"id":"bsb","name":"The Holy Bible, Berean Standard Bible","note":"Every verse quoted and opened on this page. Public domain, dedicated 2023. Courtesy credit: Berean Standard Bible, berean.bible. Read here from the site's own data/plain/bsb.","href":"https://berean.bible"},{"id":"calvin-eph","name":"John Calvin, Commentary on Galatians and Ephesians, trans. William Pringle","note":"Read directly: his comments on Ephesians 5:21–25 and 6:5 only, not the whole book. Reformed, not Baptist. Public domain.","href":"https://ccel.org/ccel/calvin/calcom41.html"},{"id":"calvin-rom","name":"John Calvin, Commentary on Romans, trans. John Owen","note":"Read directly: his comments on Romans 13:1–7 only. Reformed, not Baptist. Public domain.","href":"https://ccel.org/ccel/calvin/calcom38.html"},{"id":"gill","name":"John Gill, A Body of Practical Divinity, Book IV, chapters 1 and 4","note":"Read directly: the chapters on husband and wife and on magistrates and subjects, not the whole book. A Baptist work of doctrine, not a verse-by-verse commentary. Public domain.","href":"https://ccel.org/ccel/gill/practical.html"},{"id":"bfm","name":"The Baptist Faith and Message 2000, Articles 13, 17 and 18","note":"Consulted at bfm.sbc.net on 2026-10-30: these three articles only. Copyright Southern Baptist Convention, so short phrases only, with a link. A witness to what Baptists hold; Scripture remains the authority.","href":"https://bfm.sbc.net/bfm2000/"},{"id":"sbc-1995","name":"Southern Baptist Convention, Resolution on Racial Reconciliation, Atlanta, 1995","note":"Consulted at sbc.net on 2026-10-30: this one resolution. Short phrases only, with a link.","href":"https://www.sbc.net/resource-library/resolutions/resolution-on-racial-reconciliation-on-the-150th-anniversary-of-the-southern-baptist-convention/"}],"numbers":{"places":6,"verses":168,"letters":10,"reasons":35,"towardLord":21,"towardPerson":14,"older":10,"letterVerses":9}};
